  "description": "The Vitesse EVO is the lightest bike in the Vitus range – a true pro race bike.\n\nDesigned with minimal weight to charge up climbs, efficient stiffness to sprint and accelerate, and all-day comfort to glide through rough road surfaces with minimal fatigue, this bike will leave you fresh to challenge for the finish line.\n\nWe worked collaboratively with the professional UCI Continental Pro cycling team, An-Post CRC throughout the design and test phase of the Vitesse Evo, with a comprehensive testing and feedback programme. This allowed our designers to optimise the Vitesse EVO, achieving the perfect balance of ride characteristics to make this bike competitive in all conditions- from the spring classics, to the high mountains of Europe. The Vitesse EVO is a proven, professional race winning platform, and is the bike of choice for professional team, Vitus Pro Cycling in 2020.\n\nThe Vitesse EVO is now a disc brake only frameset, with full internal cable routing, and a UCI certified frame and fork. With semi-compact geometry and lots of flexibility in its set-up, you’re guaranteed to get the position you want. The Vitesse EVO is renowned for its composed handling being both balanced and stable, yet nimble enough to pilot through a bunch sprint.\n\nThe Vitesse Evo CRi Disc comes fitted with the high-performance Shimano Ultegra R8050 11 speed electronic groupset and Ultegra hydraulic flat mount disc brakes. To maximise aerodynamics and reduce weight, the Di2 junction box is hidden in the handlebar bar-end, allowing for easy on-the-fly adjustments, and a great clean look. For performance and reliability, the Ultegra Di2 groupset is hard to beat.\n\nThe race-proven and UCI approved Prime Carbon Black Edition 38 tubeless ready wheels feature a 38mm deep aero rim section, providing the perfect balance between low weight and aerodynamics. The Black Edition 38 combines this with a wider rim profile to create a more linear contour between the tyre and rim interface. They are paired with Hutchinson Fusion Five Performance Tubeless 25c tyres, maximising aero gains and comfort. The new Vitus Switch axles give you the option to leave the lever handle firmly secured in either wheel or remove it for extra weight saving and aero gains.\n\nThe cockpit utilises Prime’s popular Doyenne aluminium semi-aero handlebars as used by Vitus Pro Cycling. The bars feature a lightweight hydroformed shape, internal cable routing and come fitted to the performance orientated and sleek looking Zipp Service Course stem- 3D forged, and CNC machined for maximum stiffness and low weight.\n\nFinishing the bike off is a matching Zipp Service Course layback seat post, fitted with a versatile and super comfortable Prologo Kappa EVO PAS saddle.",
